% A Liana inheritance wallet: the wallet manager, or two of the family after a year, or a third party after fifteen months
%
% The Logical English twin of a Bitcoin spending policy, written by the
% Miniscript translator (InsurLE2/migration/miniscript). Who can spend the
% coin, when, and why: each rule is one spending path of the policy.
%
% Source: the Liana README
%         https://github.com/wizardsardine/liana#about
%
% The source, as written (cut into lines of 100 characters: join them for the text):
%     or(99@pk(manager),or(9@and(thresh(2,pk(spouse),pk(first_child),pk(second_child)),older(52560)),and(p
%     k(third_party),older(65535))))
%
% The source, laid out (keys and hashes by their role, <like this>):
%     or(
%       99@pk(<the wallet manager>),
%       or(
%         9@and(
%           thresh(2,
%             pk(<the spouse>),
%             pk(<the elder child>),
%             pk(<the younger child>)),
%           older(52560)),
%         and(pk(<the third party>),older(65535))))
%
% The legend (role <- key or hash as written in the source):
%     the wallet manager <- manager
%     the spouse         <- spouse
%     the elder child    <- first_child
%     the younger child  <- second_child
%     the third party    <- third_party
%
% What it says (the spending policy, by BIP 379's semantics):
%     any one of these:
%       a signature by the wallet manager
%       all of these:
%         at least 2 of these 3:
%           a signature by the spouse
%           a signature by the elder child
%           a signature by the younger child
%         the coin at least 52560 blocks old (about 365 days; older(52560))
%       all of these:
%         a signature by the third party
%         the coin at least 65535 blocks old (about 455 days; older(65535))
%
% The weights (like 99@) guide sipa's compiler towards the likelier paths;
% they do not change who can spend, and the twin leaves them out.
%
% Try it in Minsc (the policy compiled to Miniscript, Script and an address,
% in the browser): the document "the policy in Minsc" below.

the target language is: prolog.

the knowledge base liana_inheritance includes these resources:
    temporal.

the templates are:
    the coin can be spent.
    the coin was confirmed in block *a height*; scenario element.
    the spending transaction is in block *a height*; scenario element.
    the coin has been confirmed for *a number* blocks.
    the witness contains a signature by *a key*; scenario element.

